.TH ACORN-FILE-FORGE 1 "August 2026" "Acorn File Forge" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acorn-file-forge \- open and maintain Acorn media images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acorn-file-forge
.RI [ image ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Acorn File Forge is a GTK desktop application for browsing, editing,
validating and converting Acorn BBC, Electron, Archimedes and RISC OS disk,
tape, ROM and hard-drive images.
.PP
Files named on the command line are opened through the same private-copy and
format-validation path as the GTK file chooser. A matching BeebSCSI DAT and DSC
pair is treated as one image.
.PP
HFE floppy images are decoded and encoded with the bundled
HxCFloppyEmulator command-line converter, hxcfe. Clean sector-based HFE v1
images are editable and are decoded again for byte-exact verification before
download. Advanced or damaged HFE images open read-only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACORN_FILE_FORGE_DISABLE_WEBKIT_SANDBOX
Set to auto, 0 or 1. The default auto mode enables the compatibility fallback
only when Ubuntu reports its restricted unprivileged-user-namespace policy.
.TP
.B ACORN_ELKULATOR_ROOT, ACORN_BEM_ROOT, ACORN_MAME_EXECUTABLE, ACORN_MAME_ROM_PATH
Override optional native emulator and firmware locations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/acorn-file-forge/work
Private working images when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
.TP
.I ~/.config/acorn-file-forge
Owner identity and atomic client state when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed handbook is under
.IR /usr/share/doc/acorn-file-forge/ .
The HFE and HxCFE guide is
.IR /usr/share/doc/acorn-file-forge/handbook/HFE-HXC-GUIDE.md .
